      "text": "REHEARSAL FIXTURE: this text is invented to rehearse Tenantly's ingest pipeline. It is not a real law.\n\nORDINANCE NO. R-2026-REHEARSAL\n\nAN ORDINANCE LIMITING RENTAL APPLICATION FEES IN THE CITY OF CAMBRIDGE\n\nBE IT ORDAINED by the City Council of the City of Cambridge:\n\nSection 8.99.010. Application fees.\nNo landlord or agent of a landlord shall charge a prospective tenant an application fee or screening fee that exceeds fifty dollars ($50) for any rental unit in a building with five or more units.\n\nSection 8.99.020. Exemptions.\nThis chapter does not apply to a building with fewer than five units in which the owner lives.\n\nSection 8.99.030. Effective date.\nThis ordinance shall take effect on the first day of the second month next following the date of enactment.\n\nApproved November 20, 2026.",
